SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE
================================================================================

This MIT license covers ONLY the original additions that I authored from scratch
for the AMD ROCm low-VRAM port of Hunyuan3D-2.1:

  Wholly original files (entire file is mine):
    - amd-rocm-extras/run_texture.py
    - amd-rocm-extras/launch_hunyuan_unified.sh
    - amd-rocm-extras/launch_texture.sh
    - amd-rocm-extras/README.md
    - amd-rocm-extras/LICENSE          (this file)
    - amd_rocm_patches.py              (helper module at repo root)
    - README_AMD_ROCM.md
    - PORTING_GUIDE.md
    - requirements_amd.txt             (my pinned dependency selection)
    - requirements_texture.txt         (my pinned dependency selection)

  My modifications inside otherwise upstream-licensed files:
    The patch chunks (additions, deletions, edits) I introduced in:
      gradio_app.py
      hy3dpaint/utils/multiview_utils.py
      hy3dpaint/utils/pipeline_utils.py
      hy3dpaint/textureGenPipeline.py
      hy3dpaint/hunyuanpaintpbr/unet/attn_processor.py
      hy3dpaint/hunyuanpaintpbr/unet/modules.py
      hy3dpaint/custom_rasterizer/setup.py
    are released under MIT, but ONLY my patch portions — not the surrounding
    upstream code. The combined files as a whole remain subject to the
    Tencent Hunyuan 3D 2.1 Community License Agreement (see the repository-root
    LICENSE file). Anyone using these files must comply with both licenses.

  Derivative HIP sources:
    The files
      hy3dpaint/custom_rasterizer/lib/custom_rasterizer_kernel/grid_neighbor_hip.cpp
      hy3dpaint/custom_rasterizer/lib/custom_rasterizer_kernel/rasterizer_gpu.hip
      hy3dpaint/custom_rasterizer/lib/custom_rasterizer_kernel/rasterizer_hip.cpp
      hy3dpaint/custom_rasterizer/lib/custom_rasterizer_kernel/rasterizer_hip.h
    were generated from upstream Tencent CUDA sources using `hipify-perl -inplace`.
    They are mechanical translations of Tencent code and therefore derivative works.
    Any original adjustments I made to them are released under MIT, but the
    underlying translated structure inherits from the original CUDA sources and
    remains subject to the Tencent Hunyuan 3D 2.1 Community License Agreement.

  Hunyuan3D-2.1 itself:
    The original Hunyuan3D-2.1 source code, weights, configuration, datasets,
    and assets remain the property of Tencent and are licensed under the
    "Tencent Hunyuan 3D 2.1 Community License Agreement". See LICENSE and
    Notice.txt at the repository root for the full upstream license terms.
    This MIT license does NOT relicense, redistribute, or modify any of the
    upstream Tencent code or weights.

